.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_RAW_STREAM 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_RAW_STREAM \- Specify whether this audio device should do audio processing.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_RAW_STREAM \(dqSDL_AUDIO_DEVICE_RAW_STREAM\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Some operating systems perform echo cancellation, gain control, and noise reduction as needed\[char46] If your application already handles these, you can set this hint to prevent the OS from doing additional audio processing\[char46]
.PP
This corresponds to the WASAPI audio option
.BR AUDCLNT_STREAMOPTIONS_RAW \[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: audio processing can be done by the OS\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: audio processing is done by the application\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

